  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Vieille Ferme is a 4-star campsite at 296 boulevard des Groules in Villeneuve-Loubet, in the middle of the Vaugrenier departmental nature park according to its official website. It covers 28,000 m² of wooded grounds, with 119 hedged, semi-shaded pitches for tents, caravans or motorhomes, and 32 air-conditioned chalets with covered terraces.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The official website states: pets are accepted on a leash with an up-to-date vaccination record, except category 1 and 2 dogs. It does not mention a surcharge, a maximum number of dogs per pitch or a size limit, does not say whether the rule is the same for pitches and chalets, and does not list any dog-specific facilities.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call the campsite on +33 4 93 33 41 44 before booking to ask about the dog fee, the number of dogs allowed and the rule for chalets if you travel with more than one dog or a large one.</div>

      <h2>Dates and services</h2>
      <p>The campsite closed on 16 October 2026 and reopens on 1 February 2027. The pools open from 3 April to 30 September 2027; the site does not say whether dogs may go near them. On site: bread and pastry service and a snack-pizzeria from April to October, a laundry, heated sanitary blocks, a play area, a boules pitch and a motorhome service point. Wi-Fi is paid.</p>

      <h2>Getting there and nearby</h2>
      <p>Biot railway station is 1 km away, a bus stop (Nice-Cannes line) 200 m, and Nice airport 12 km. An Intermarché and a Carrefour Market are 1.5 km away. For walks with your dog, the Vaugrenier departmental park around the campsite is a natural starting point: ask the park or the Villeneuve-Loubet tourist office (villeneuve-tourisme.com) about leash rules there.</p>
    </div>

